    'tool.peer_delegate.names' => 'Neighbours a task can go to: %s. Addresses, keys and connections — peer_directory (when the role has the permission peers).',
    'tool.peer_directory.about' => 'The directory of the network of agents (the role permission peers): me — name, card address, transport, WebSocket address, fingerprint and public key; the neighbours I connect to — address, transport, WebSocket address, fingerprint, public key, whether a connection is open; the live connections both ways; to people also the agents I let in. counts: total — how many agents I know, visible — how many of them are shown (the owner hid the rest). With peer — the directory of that neighbour, by its method ListPeers. There are no tokens and private keys here: to connect to an agent one needs its entrance token and its owner letting one in (/peer allow).',
    'tool.peer_directory.peer' => 'The name of a neighbour: ask for its directory (the method ListPeers). It answers only when the role it gave me has the permission peers. Without peer — my own directory.',
    'tool.peer_directory.no_right' => 'The directory of the network is for a role with the permission peers; an owner of the agent gives it (/role set <role> permissions …).',
    'tool.peer_delegate.nuzhna_zadacha_task' => 'A task is required: task.',
